# Rally-identification accuracy feedback

## Scope

This report covers only rally-identification correctness in the current source and the two
supplied golden datasets:

- `samples/test_input_1.mp4` with `samples/test_output_rally_1.txt`
- `samples/test_input_2.mp4` with `samples/test_output_rally_2.txt`

The acceptance rule is exactly one output per annotated logical point, with start and end
independently within 2.0 seconds of the annotation. An annotated fault/let may use either
the original-serve or retry-serve start, but must remain one output point.

## Current result

Both datasets pass the acceptance rule with the default `RallyConfig()` and player
detection enabled:

| Dataset | Annotated points | Detected points | Boundary result |
|---|---:|---:|---|
| 1 | 9 | 9 | all starts and ends within 2.0 seconds |
| 2 | 9 | 9 | all starts and ends within 2.0 seconds |

