## Confirmed issues fixed

- Accuracy mode no longer drops lower-ranked proposal regions before TrackNet evaluation.
- Short and one-contact hypotheses survive abstention instead of being rejected solely by
  audio duration.
- Temporally compatible ball-track fragments are evaluated together, and audio-aligned
  ball endpoints remove post-point pickup noise without allowing an uncalibrated local
  fragment to erase most of a long rally.
- Serve evidence now requires ordered pre-contact and outgoing ball motion. Stationary
  baseline-player and overhead-pose signals support the decision without independently
  turning pickups, handoffs, score calls, or walking into match points.
- The match decoder groups same-side fault/retry and split-rally fragments into one logical
  point, rejects match candidates without a confirmed serve, and anchors a compact serve
  fragment that directly precedes a long exchange.
- Point ends retain the requested real-video buffer; no artificial black transition is
  inserted.

## Remaining confirmed failures

None in the supplied golden evaluation. This result is evidence for these two independently
annotated videos, not a claim that unannotated camera layouts or match conditions cannot
expose new errors. New accuracy issues should be added here only when supported by a
reproducible code path and independent annotation.

## Verification

- Full fast suite: `184 passed, 2 skipped`.
- Fresh dataset-2 end-to-end gate: `1 passed`.
- Fresh dataset-1 model evidence replayed through the final deterministic match decoder:
  all 9 points pass the same boundary assertion.
- Combined golden sidecar gate: `10 passed`.
